@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <div class="text-center mb-14">
        <p class="text-stone text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase mb-2" style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;">The project</p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-5xl font-bold text-ink mb-3">About Sugbo</h1>
        <div class="ornament text-gold">— ✦ —</div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-body space-y-6" style="font-family:'Crimson Pro',serif;font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.85;color:#1a1208;">
        <p class="dropcap">
            <strong>Sugbo</strong> — the old name for Cebu — is a free, non-commercial archive dedicated to preserving and sharing the documented history of one of Southeast Asia's oldest continuously inhabited cities.
        </p>
        <p>
            The project was born from a simple observation: Cebu's extraordinary history — as first contact point of Spanish colonialism, as seat of the oldest Catholic relic in the Philippines, as site of the first Filipino act of resistance against foreign conquest — is unevenly documented in accessible, readable form.
        </p>
        <p>
            Sugbo aims to be something between academic monographs and Wikipedia: rigorously grounded in the historical record, but written for the educated general reader — the student writing a school paper, the traveler curious about the city, the Cebuano who wants to know the story behind the cross their grandmother prays to.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-sienna/8 border-l-4 border-sienna/60 pl-6 py-4 my-8">
            <p class="font-display text-xl italic text-sienna">"The past is never dead. It's not even past."</p>
            <p class="text-stone text-sm mt-2 tracking-wide" style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;">— William Faulkner</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mt-10 mb-3">What We Publish</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-base">
            <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-gold mt-1">✦</span><span><strong>Stories &amp; Essays</strong> — narrative histories written for a general audience.</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-gold mt-1">✦</span><span><strong>Historical Photographs</strong> — archival images in the public domain.</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-gold mt-1">✦</span><span><strong>Primary Documents</strong> — maps, decrees, chronicles, and official records.</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Contribute</h2>
        <p>
            If you have old photographs, family documents, oral histories, or expertise in Cebuano history, we welcome contributions.
        </p>
        <p>
            Write to us at: <a href="mailto:archive@sugbochronicles.ph" class="text-sienna hover:underline">archive@sugbochronicles.ph</a>
        </p>

        <div class="ruled mt-10"></div>
        <p class="text-stone text-sm text-center" style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;letter-spacing:0.05em;">
            Sugbo: Chronicles of Cebu is an independent educational project.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>